      "description": "Watch Besiktas vs FC Midtjylland highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 23, 2026. On July 23, 2026 , the UEFA Europa League stage was set for a high-stakes encounter as Besiktas hosted FC Midtjylland . The atmosphere was electric as both teams looked to establish dominance in this prestigious European competition. Early Dismissal Changes the Dynamic The match began with high intensity, but the tactical plans of FC Midtjylland were thrown into disarray after just 15 minutes. A serious foul by Friday Etim left the referee with no choice but to brandish a red card , forcing the visitors to play with ten men for the vast majority of the game. This early exit prompted an immediate tactical adjustment, with Valdemar Byskov making way for Denil Castillo as the Danish side tried to shore up their defenses. Kokcu Breaks the Deadlock Capitalizing on the numerical advantage, Besiktas began to dictate the tempo. The pressure culminated in the 26th minute when Vaclav Cerny found Orkun Kokcu in a dangerous position. From well outside the box, Kokcu unleashed a powerful right-footed strike that flew past the goalkeeper, igniting celebrations across the stadium. The Turkish side continued to control the ball throughout the remainder of the first half , heading into the break with the momentum firmly on their side. Tactical Battle in the Second Half The second half saw a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked to influence the outcome. Besiktas introduced fresh legs in Milot Rashica and Semih Kilicsoy , while Midtjylland brought on Martin Erlic and Gue-Sung Cho to stay competitive. A late concern for the hosts arose when Tiago Djalo suffered an injury in the 78th minute, leading to the introduction of Emmanuel Agbadou . Despite several late attempts and tactical shifts, the initial breakthrough remained the defining moment as the referee blew the final whistle at 90+4'."
